Just a reminder to readers/posters of comp.os.linux.announce.

First of all, we're no longer crossposting to comp.os.linux. If you
don't get c.o.l.a at your site, encourage your news admins to add
it, or join the ANNOUNCE channel of the Linux-Activists mailing list.

Secondly: If you're posting announcements such as
	"Hi. I've just uploaded FooBar v4.2 to sunsite and tsx-11...."
and don't specify in your posting WHAT the program "FooBar" is or what it 
does, then we will reject the article until you provide more information. 
I've seen too many postings announcing new software or patches that don't
give a brief (i.e. one sentence or so) rundown of the software. 

For the most part, we all know what "GCC" and "Linux" and so on are. But if
you're announcing obscure software that most of us haven't heard about, please
provide a short summary of what the software does. Lars and I will try our
best to add this information if you fail to provide it--- but we can only do
that if WE know what the software does. :)

And, last thing: Remember to provide a Keywords: header line in all of your
postings. I see a lot of announcements come through without Keywords: in
the header, and Lars and I have to add them. 

I'm glad to see that c.o.l.a is getting heavy use these days. Thanks everyone!

