Somebody on comp.os.linux suggested we needed a common, front-end for
the growing number of file system checkers and builders under Linux.
Since I agreed and had a little free time on my hands, I wrote one.
All it really does is figure out which file system type should be used
and executes the appropriate program, but it does allow you to simply
type 'fsck /dev/xyz' without regard to the file system type in most
cases.  Mkfs is similarly supported, but is (IMO) of dubious value.

Look for /pub/Linux/Incoming/fsutil-1.0.tar.Z on sunsite.unc.edu.

