I have put my driver for the Sony CDU-31A CDROM drive on
sunsite.unc.edu in the incoming directory.  This will drive the newer
Sony interface (not SCSI) drives for audio and data.  It is named
sonycd-0.1.tar.Z.

I just talked with Sony (after finishing the driver) and they say this
will NOT work with the older CDU-535.  The CDU-31A is Sony's newer
bigger faster better drive that came out recently.  I am getting the
programmer's manual for the 535, but I'm not holding my breath about
compatibility.  If someone wants to try it out with a CDU-535, I would
like to hear the results.  I will try to add support for the 535 in
future versions, but since I don't have one, I can't promise anything.

The driver is mostly complient with the Sun driver (as described in
the cdrom.h include file under include/linux) and will mount CDROMs
and play audio CDs.  I have included xcdplayer with it; the stuff to
play CDs seems to work fine but a bug in the title stuff will cause a
core dump.  Since that is not related to the driver, I have not been
too concerned with it.  I will try to fix that as soon as I have time.

