The new version 1.1 of xsysinfo is available at the following sites:

    sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/linux/Incoming/xsysinfo-1.1.tar.Z

and tsx-11.mit.edu:/incoming/xsysinfo-1.1.tar.Z	(I hope it will be moved soon
    to a dir, where it is world readable)

xsysinfo is an X application to display some Linux kernel
parameters in graphical form. It is like a mix of top, free and xload
with the difference that the values are shown in form of a horizontal bar.
The displayed values are: CPU load, CPU idle, memory and swap sizes

Changes since last version:

	- it uses the proc fs to obtain kernel params

	- new, more detailed memory info

	- supports up to 8 swap partitions/files

	- gauges can be disabled

xsysinfo requires at least Linux 0.99pl2 with proc fs. The included binary
is compiled for shared libs 4.2 and XFree-1.1 with 2.1 shared libs.

Have fun watching the kernel work...

Gabor

